# Backend Rules

Extends [`always.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/always.mdc). Adds backend-specific guidance.

## API conventions

- All routes under `/api/v1/*`. Major version bumps require ADR.
- Zod (TS) / Pydantic (Py) at every route boundary - request AND response.
- Errors are typed `AppError` subclasses with HTTP status mapped at the boundary.
- No bare `throw new Error()`. No catching and silently swallowing.

## Data access

- ORM only (Prisma / SQLAlchemy). No raw SQL except for migrations and rare read-only analytics.
- All queries parameterized. Never string-concat user input into SQL.
- N+1 queries are bugs - use eager loading / `select_related` / `include`.

## Async

- Async I/O everywhere (no sync DB calls in async handlers).
- All external calls have timeouts (default 5s).
- Long-running work goes to a queue (BullMQ / Celery), not inline in HTTP handler.

## Logging

- Structured JSON via pino (Node) / structlog (Python).
- Correlation ID per request, propagated to all downstream calls.
- Log levels: `debug` (verbose), `info` (notable events), `warn` (recoverable), `error` (failed).
- Never log secrets, tokens, or full request bodies that may contain PII.

## Auth

- JWT short-lived (<= 15 min) + refresh token (httpOnly, secure, sameSite=lax).
- Refresh rotation: each refresh issues a new refresh token; old one invalid.
- Authz checked on EVERY endpoint, not just login. Use middleware/decorator pattern.
- Deny by default; allow by explicit role.

## Don't

- Don't trust client-supplied IDs - re-lookup server-side and check authz.
- Don't return internal error details in 5xx responses (security leak).
- Don't make HTTP calls without timeout + retry policy.
- Don't import from `apps/web/*` (cross-app boundary).
